      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Illusory Copies",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "arcane",
        "illusion",
        "visual"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency once per day\n\n---\n\nEffect Blune calls into existence 1d4+2 illusory copies of himself, which dance around him and copy his every movement, making it almost impossible to pinpoint the true Blune.\n\nAny attack that would hit Blune has a random chance of hitting an illusory copy instead. This effect lasts for up to 1 minute or until all the copies are destroyed or Blune is incapacitated.\n\nOnce a copy is hit, it's destroyed. If an attack roll fails to hit Blune's AC but doesn't critically fail, it destroys a copy but has no additional effect (even if the attack would normally have an effect on a failure). If an attack roll is a critical success and would hit a copy, the copy is destroyed and the attack roll becomes a success against Blune.\n\nOnce all the copies are destroyed, this ability ends.",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "day"
      }
    },
